            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A coiled tubing unit (10) includes a coiled tubing assembly (18) and a slickline assembly (26) sharing an axis of rotation (58) with the coiled tubing assembly. A shaft (54) of the coiled tubing assembly (18) is received by bearings (46) on a slickline drum (40) of the slickline assembly (26) and extends through an interior of the slickline drum. A swivel joint connection (48) is rotatably affixed on an end of the main shaft as it exits the interior of the slickline drum, thus allowing for introduction of fluid or cabling into the main shaft and into the coiled tubing. The coiled tubing drum and slickline drum can rotate independently and are powered independently of each other. The coiled tubing and slickline assemblies are preferably affixed to a removable module (14), the removable module being positioned on a skid (12) having a power unit (30) and appropriate controls.</p>
            </abstract>
